# Real example calls in docs

When writing or updating function help headers, README usage blocks, or API docs:

- Always include at least one **Example** that is a full, copy-pasteable call
- Use real lab paths (e.g. `Y:\Data\Feno\20260715`, `Y:\Projects\dPul-MIP\Feno\Behavior_analysis\`), never `/path/to/...` or bare basenames alone
- Prefer the canonical session call:

```matlab
out = ma1_analyze_reaches_session( ...
    'Y:\Data\Feno\20260715', ...
    'Y:\Projects\dPul-MIP\Feno\Behavior_analysis\');
```

- Abstract Usage signatures are fine *in addition* to real Examples; never replace Examples with only signatures
